 - Improvements to `TimeSeries` :
   - `__pow__` now supports raising to negative powers (as series, arrays or scalars). E.g. `series ** (-2)`. [#3298](https://github.com/unit8co/darts/pull/3298) by [Gabriel Demetrios Lafis](https://github.com/galafis).
   - `__truediv__` now supports dividing by zeros (as series, arrays or scalars). E.g. `series / 0.` [#3298](https://github.com/unit8co/darts/pull/3298) by [Gabriel Demetrios Lafis](https://github.com/galafis).
+  - `values()`, `univariate_values()` and `to_dataframe()` now accept an `agg` parameter to aggregate the samples of a stochastic series (`"mean"`, `"median"`, or a quantile as a float between 0 and 1) instead of silently extracting a single sample. Calling `values()` or `univariate_values()` on a stochastic series without specifying `sample` or `agg` now logs a warning, since only the first sample is returned.
 
 **Fixed**
 
